wer station and a 100W solar panel, making it suitable for home emergency backup, camping, and road trips. The 25-pound unit provides 1,800W of continuous AC output, can power up to 11 devices, supports UPS switching within 10 milliseconds, and is rated for more than 4,000 battery cycles. AC charging reaches 80% in approximately 45 minutes and full capacity in about 70 minutes, while the included panel takes roughly seven hours under favorable conditions. Reviewers praise its portability, quiet operation, app, and high output. However, the current price is $79 above its previous Black Friday low of $550. Buyers needing only phone charging may prefer a smaller station, and the 100W panel is relatively slow for the battery\u2019s capacity. The panel ships separately, and advertised surge or Power Lifting figures should not be confused with continuous output.","ref_id":{"turn_index":765116,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":12},"pub_date":1786975894.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/eO6vvmhrl712x24yCRSMDzChc9Wny4RWvE2TfetOVkoSUY679MF9In0GGJnaKq0vmz5QAS4FY_SBHgNTpV-z35UL9rpNSyNhb8JkSP_mg5sECldhWK9ZYfp8oOcu6kW4","attribution":"www.techradar.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.goodhousekeeping.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/home/a71395320/jackery-home-generator-memorial-sale/","title":"Under $1,700: Our Top-Tested Solar Generator-With Panels Included","snippet":"Good Housekeeping names the Jackery HomePower 3000 its top-tested solar generator after evaluating more than 20 portable power stations. The emissions-free unit is currently offered with two 200-watt solar panels for under $1,700, representing a 43% discount and $1,300 in savings. It delivers 3,600 watts continuously and up to 7,200 watts in surge mode, enough to power a full-size refrigerator for several days, and includes five AC outlets and four USB ports. Its LiFePO4 battery reached a full charge in two hours from a wall outlet